Cabinet","time":"4.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.peterborough.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-29","committee":"Shareholder Cabinet Committee","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.peterborough.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-30","committee":"Economy, Inclusive Growth and Environment Scrutiny Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed; Extraordinary","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.peterborough.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-01","committee":"Prevention, Independence and Resilience Scrutiny Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.peterborough.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-14","committee":"Council","time":"5.00 pm","status":"New; Honorary Aldermen","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.peterborough.gov.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-07-22","committee":"Economy, Inclusive Growth and Environment Scrutiny Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed; Rescheduled","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.peterborough.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-23","committee":"Sustainable Future City Council Scrutiny Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.peterborough.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-29","committee":"Council","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.peterborough.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-08-25","committee":"Cabinet","time":"2.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.peterborough.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-17","committee":"Sustainable Future City Council Scrutiny Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.peterborough.gov.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Peterborough faces \u00a37.9m overspend as children's care costs rise","lead":"Peterborough Council faces a \u00a37.9m overspend in the current financial year that will reduce its general reserves to \u00a36.7m, down from \u00a310.5m at the start, leaving the council with a minimal financial buffer. The largest pressure is children's residential placements, costing \u00a33.2m more than budgeted because average weekly costs have risen to \u00a39,000 from \u00a36,500. The number of placements has increased to 47 from a budgeted 41. The council also faces a \u00a32.7m income shortfall at Clare Lodge, a secure unit for children, which has been unable to operate at full occupancy due to restrictions imposed by the children's regulator OFSTED. Agency staff in children's social care are running \u00a30.6m over budget.","iso":"2026-09-17","paper_title":"June 26 BCR SFCC","paper_url":"https://peterborough.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s60459/60459.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-23","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"Appendix C: Internal Audit Progress Report","paper_url":"https://peterborough.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s60640/60640.pdf","headline":"Council appoints two new Senior Auditors to strengthen internal audit function","detail":"Peterborough Council has appointed 2 new Senior Auditors who started in September 2026. The council is actively working to move away from reliance on external audit contracts and build permanent internal audit capacity.","category":"people","matters":"Investment in internal audit function demonstrates commitment to governance improvement. Building internal audit capacity suggests confidence in remediating the identified control issues.","figures":"2 new Senior Auditors","quote":"Following successful interviews, PCC has been able to appoint 2 Senior Auditors who started in September 2026.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-23","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"Appendix C: Internal Audit Progress Report","paper_url":"https://peterborough.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s60640/60640.pdf","headline":"Only 51% of agreed audit actions have been completed, with completion rate declining","detail":"Across 113 total agreed internal audit actions, only 57 (51%) have been completed as of 31 August 2026. A further 41 (36%) are in progress, 11 (10%) have not started, and 4 (3%) have unknown status. The completion rate declined from 53% in July 2026.","category":"governance","matters":"Low and declining audit action completion rates indicate the council is not effectively remediating known control weaknesses, suggesting systemic governance challenges.","figures":"113 total actions: 57 completed (51%), 41 in progress (36%), 11 not started (10%), 4 unknown (3%); completion rate declined from 53% in July","quote":"% August  51% 36% 10% 3%","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-23","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"Appendix C: Internal Audit Progress Report","paper_url":"https://peterborough.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s60640/60640.pdf","headline":"Starters/Leavers/Movers payroll audit from June 2025 now 14 months overdue with 7 actions not started","detail":"The Starters/Leavers/Movers audit received a Limited assurance rating and was due in June 2025. As of 31 August 2026, 30 agreed actions remain unresolved, with 7 not yet started, 9 in progress, and 14 completed.","category":"audit","matters":"This audit concerns payroll controls and HR reconciliation. A Limited assurance rating from an overdue audit with actions still unstarted raises concerns about whether payroll controls are operating effectively.","figures":"30 actions: 14 completed, 9 in progress, 7 not started; audit now 14 months past due date","quote":"Starters/Leavers/Movers 3 Limited Jun 25 30 14 9 7","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-23","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"Appendix C: Internal Audit Progress Report","paper_url":"https://peterborough.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s60640/60640.pdf","headline":"Health and Safety audit from August 2023 has completed only 5 of 22 required actions after three years","detail":"The Health & Safety consultant audit dated August 2023 identified 22 required actions. As of 31 August 2026, only 5 have been completed and 17 remain unstarted, leaving 77% of corrective actions unimplemented.","category":"audit","matters":"Health and Safety is a core duty of an employer. A three-year-old audit with the vast majority of actions unimplemented indicates serious gaps in operational governance and risk management.","figures":"22 actions: 5 completed, 17 not started","quote":"Health & Safety 2 consultant report Aug 23 22 5 17","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-23","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"Appendix C: Internal Audit Progress Report","paper_url":"https://peterborough.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s60640/60640.pdf","headline":"PCI Compliance audit from August 2023 remains largely unimplemented after two years","detail":"The PCI Compliance audit received a Limited assurance rating in August 2023. As of 31 August 2026, only 2 of 6 required actions have been completed, with 4 remaining unstarted, meaning two-thirds of corrective actions remain unimplemented.","category":"audit","matters":"PCI compliance is critical for data security and payment card data protection. A Limited assurance finding with most actions unimplemented represents a significant ongoing security and control risk.","figures":"6 actions: 2 completed, 4 not started","quote":"PCI Compliance  Limited Aug 23 6 2  4","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-17"},"name":"Peterborough UA","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-20","since_iso":"2026-08-21","distress":true,"headline":"Children's Social Care statutory complaints are being upheld at higher rates than the council anticipated.","lead":"An elevated uphold rate in Children's Social Care statutory complaints signals either decision-making quality issues or service delivery problems that could trigger audit findings or regulatory scrutiny.","also":["9 other findings in this window","1 paper caught"],"watch":"Audit Committee on 2026-09-23","n_findings":10,"n_documents":1,"top_paper_title":"Q1 PCC corporate performance report August 2026 (FINALv2)","top_paper_url":"https://peterborough.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s60458/60458.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":160,"news_drafts_total":1}}